      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from the biblical town Dimonah, preserved in the Arabic name Harabat Umm Dumna, and means “shepherdess” in Hebrew.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        13,
        6
      ],
