      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Dimona",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Shimon Peres Negev Nuclear Research Center, known as the Dimona Reactor, sits 13 km southeast of the city and began operation in 1958.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dimona",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Dimona hosts one of Israel’s largest diamond processing hubs, while the nearby Ashalim Solar Power Station showcases the region’s shift toward renewable energy.",
